./xmodel/grok-vanrijn.md:117:**Net on row 10.** He has not found a JC2 proof, an HC4 proof, or a reason to raise 6.5. He has executed the case-tree the adjudication predicted would be the *modal* outcome ("hard coupled-layer case tree"), and inside it he isolated a clean unit obstruction that reduces one moving-kernel packet to JC2. That is information-yield of the kind Sol scored, obtained independently, and it is the one HC4 object worth replaying before we spend campaign days on Ni's quartic. It does not change the endgame probability: leftover packets still have to *be* JC2.
