xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:1:**VERDICT: SOUND — Q/max is the unique uniform repair of Notation 3.5; Q plus printed Statement 3.17(ii) and Proposition 9.3(e) force E5; CONJECTURE \(U_{7C}\) is a new assertion that no printed or promoted fact in the audited chain proves; the 17-cell Q+E5 book is the sound conservative object under the filed census perimeter.**
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:5:Claims under review: (1) P/coarse at a doubly realized vertex is incoherent — it yields nonintegral \(D_{h,F}=\kappa_F d_{h,F}\), contradicting printed Statement 3.8, and conflicts with Proposition 5.5 — hence Q/jump/max \(\kappa_F=\nu_F\kappa_G/\nu_G\) is forced; (2) Q forces the E5 transport identities via printed Statement 3.17(ii) + Proposition 9.3(e), so the printed \(\nu_F\) denominators in Proposition 9.3(g),(h) are wrong unless \(\nu_F=\nu_G\); (3) the 2-cell book needs a new assertion CONJECTURE \(U_{7C}\) (\(\nu_F=\nu_G\) on the relevant case-III edges), which no printed/promoted fact proves; an exact polynomial model shows the definitions permit \(\nu_F\neq\nu_G\) (not a Keller pair, so \(U_{7C}\) is not refuted). Consequence: 17-cell book = sound conservative object.
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:6:Attacks: (a) replay the Statement 3.8 integrality argument and construct a nonintegral \(D_{h,F}\) witness under P at an actual doubly realized vertex; (b) verify the E5 derivation line by line against `refs/sigray_full.pdf` (the likeliest failure is a misread of which objects 9.3(e) transports); (c) check the polynomial model against every local hypothesis it claims; (d) hunt Statements 9.6–9.11 and the audited chain for anything that would prove \(U_{7C}\); (e) check whether the decisive-experiment spec actually discriminates \(U_{7C}\) and is fleet-runnable as written.
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:14:### 1. Severity: clear — Claim 1 holds. Uniform P is incoherent; Q/max is the unique uniform repair of Notation 3.5
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:17:- Claim: at a doubly realized vertex the two Notation 3.5 presentations give \(\kappa_F(P)=L_0=\kappa_G/\nu_G\) and \(\kappa_F(Q)=\nu_F L_0=\nu_F\kappa_G/\nu_G\); a global P convention produces nonintegral \(D_{h,F}\) and contradicts printed Statement 3.8 and the \(c=0\) proof of Proposition 5.5; Q/max is the unique uniform repair.
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:20:  **Printed Notation 3.5 is P-ambiguous.** Verbatim p.12: “Assume \(F=I_P(u)\) for some \(P\) … Set \(\kappa_F:=\kappa/e_j\), where \(\alpha_j\le u<\alpha_{j+1}\).” Two presentations of the same vertex can (and in case III do) give two values. The lattice identities (1) are the definitions: adjoining \(P\)’s jump at \(v\) multiplies the common index \(L_0\) by \(\nu_G\), so \(\kappa_G=\nu_G L_0\); \(Q\)’s jump at \(u\) multiplies it by \(\nu_F\), so \(\kappa_F(Q)=\nu_F L_0\).
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:37:  Same vertex, same convention: \(h=xy(xy^3-1)\) has \(d_{h,F}=2/3\), so \(D_{h,F}^{P}=2/3\notin\mathbb Z\); the coordinate \(y\) itself has \(d_{y,F}=-1/3\). Q-values are the integers \(4\), \(2\), \(-1\). This is a genuine Statement 3.8 failure under a uniform P-reading. It is not a td-7 book vertex (attack (a) below).
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:41:  **Notation 3.11 is corroboration, not a second proof.** It selects a branch realizing the maximal \(V_{1,a}\) point of \(I_P([0,u])\) immediately before defining \(D_{h,F}:=\kappa_F d_{h,F}\), and at a case-III \(F\) that maximal point is \(u\). It does not say “re-evaluate \(\kappa_F\) through this \(Q\).” The note’s wording is accurate.
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:43:  **What is forced.** Among the two Notation 3.5 presentation-values, only Q/max is a uniform global convention compatible with printed Statement 3.8, with the integer \(\bar\kappa\) the thesis itself uses (Statement 9.4 p.49: \(\kappa_G(\pi(G)-1)\in\mathbb N\); every printed Q-datum in 9.6–9.11), and with Proposition 5.5 at poles. A P-only-at-nonpole-III split is not refuted by a pre-§9 pointwise theorem; it is also not a reading Notation 3.5 supplies, and it is unusable by the promoted integer Q-data/N1 book. The note does not overclaim this.
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:48:- Attack: is \(D_{h,F}\) forced nonintegral under P at an *actual* doubly realized vertex of *our books*? Construct the witness.
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:51:  What *can* be said about a hypothetical realization of a book class-C merge: the merge is doubly realized by definition of case III / class C, N1 gives \(\gcd(\bar\kappa^Q,\nu)=1\), and (1c) then gives \(\bar\kappa^P=\bar\kappa^Q/\nu\) with exact denominator \(\nu\ge 2\). That already contradicts the thesis-wide integer decoration (Statement 9.4, every printed Q-datum) without needing a polynomial. For Statement 3.8 itself one still needs a concrete \(d_{h,F}\); the model supplies one, the books do not.
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:125:  **Consequence.** Deleting the 15 unequal-index cells requires \(U_{7C}\). Without it, the conservative work queue under the filed P0/P3/arrival/closure/budget hypotheses is the promoted 17-cell / 238 raw / 233 dedup book at `BOOK-OFFAXIS.md:750`. The 2-cell / 49 dedup restriction at `:790` is the sub-book after adjoining \(U_{7C}\). Census numbers were not re-enumerated here; they were already hostile-replayed in `xmodel/grok-census11a-review.md`. “Unconditionally” in the review prompt overstates the note: the 17-cell *count* is perimeter-conditional; what is unconditional relative to the printed thesis plus Q is that the 15 cells cannot be killed at the proved tier.
