xmodel/sol-toric.md:176:The present pilot fixes ((s_1,s_2,w_1,w_2)=(+,+,1,1)). A contradiction there would kill only that fiber unless a separate torus-rescaling argument made it uniform. A global nonlinear kill must retain the nonzero (w_1,w_2) parameters or certify all four sign branches and all relevant radical/scale components. No tail coordinate may be saturated merely for convenience; tails can legitimately be zero.
xmodel/sol-toric.md:186:This hierarchy is theoretically complete for **emptiness**: by the Hilbert Nullstellensatz, if the characteristic-zero affine variety is empty, some finite degree contains a certificate (1\in(F_1,\ldots,F_{76})). It is not a constructive convergence theorem for nonempty varieties; a consistent tier supplies neither a point nor a bounded degree at which one will appear.
