xmodel/sol-lateral.md:139:The classical LND reformulation asks whether the canonical inverse-Jacobian derivations are all locally nilpotent; see, for example, [Derksen's notes, Theorem 5.9](https://sites.lsa.umich.edu/hderksen/wp-content/uploads/sites/614/2018/09/LND1.pdf). Public work on the new 3D example has studied its weighted \(\mathbb G_m\)-quotient, projections, graph models, and invariant rings; [Shaska](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.20210) in fact explains why direct graded/equivariant descent does not produce a plane counterexample. I found no attempt to choose **one noncanonical triangular target \(\mathbb G_a\)-action and test whether its lift is again a \(\mathbb G_a\)-action**.
