xmodel/sol-lateral.md:311:A \(p\)-adic approach to JC is not new: [van den Essen-Lipton](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpaa.2014.09.018) gives a finite-field/unimodularity reformulation. Motivic/arc-space change of variables is also standard; see [Denef-Loeser](https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9803039). I found no application that converts a candidate JC resolution/tower into a **positive cylinder-mass ledger at infinity**. The campaign's current ledgers count Euler characteristic, branch degree, and residue; none counts Haar mass shell by shell.
