xmodel/grok-h29-review.md:480:## Residual nits (do not flip any claim)
xmodel/sol-td11-review.md:5:This is a break of the theorem/certificate, not an exhibited tower survivor. The local packet arithmetic, the four advertised near misses, and the direct 11-A `5/8` kill all replay. What fails is the universal perimeter needed to pass from those local facts to every synchronized td-11 class-B/C configuration and to arbitrary NF-D depth.
xmodel/sol-td11-review.md:71:The OB-8 gate at `cases/tower_td11.py:449-461` checks one leaf maximum, a small gcd identity, and a literal `True`. It does not enumerate even the direct 16 rows, much less the 129 nested rows or their emitted frames. Its cap-intersection argument is conditional on the relevant vertices remaining simultaneously alive. No restriction-of-ladder or global-first-death lemma establishes that condition through an inner merge; the source scope identifies precisely this local-to-global step as conjectural (`xmodel/sol-td11-13-scope.md:177-200,235-250`).
xmodel/sol-td11-review.md:79:Those are the same objects at sufficiently large depth. NF-D says the live td-11 branch pads both pole chains in step with `Pi_1=Pi_2`, and specifically gives `Pi=5^k` on both poles (`NF-D.md:183-193,216-227`). Only finitely many letters can remain above `theta*` (`NF-Z.md:124-162`), so sufficiently deep repeated-5 stacks have sub-`theta*` tails on both chains. NF-Z defines that exact situation as multi-word deep coexistence and explains the missing cross-branch aliveness/nested-exponent gcd coupling (`NF-Z.md:407-440`). Equality of the two total products does not prove that coupling.
xmodel/sol-td11-review.md:81:The gate contains no cross-branch deep-zone check: OB4 tests quotient equality/factorability, X3 tests a local Case-A divisor, and the theorem aggregate merely combines those booleans. `cases/nfd_check.py` still correctly prints `D(11-A)=D(11-B)=D(11-C)=OPEN` for the infinite equalized family.
xmodel/sol-td11-review.md:104:This synchronized current-state branch is absent from OB4's entry-level `(1,1)`/`(1,M_entry)` characterization. Its competing gap is `2/5 < 3/5=gap(X)`, and the abstract cap argument appears to kill it; the point is that the claimed all-`mu` characterization/gate never tested it.
xmodel/sol-td11-review.md:106:Second, there is a complete budget-feasible synchronized/E5F route candidate omitted by the budget-5 cell map:
xmodel/sol-td11-review.md:154:A4 is also a finite sample, not its advertised all-route proof: `cases/tower_td11.py:130-140` tests letters below 16 and stack depth at most 2. The symbolic valuation argument is valid, so this is test-strength errata rather than an escape.
