xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:2824:Dim-2 keeps proving the statements that are true (GMC(2), Shaska for every weight sign, no graded plane CE). Every known \(n\ge 3\) mechanism dies in the plane (Picard/\(d=3\) needle, no tangent-sweep, no graded escape). Eighty-five years without an example is evidence. Residue-A is the best formal candidate I have seen in this literature, but “passes the printed list” is exactly Theorem O, and an étale non-proper degree-6 endomorphism of \(\mathbb{A}^2\) is the thing JC2 says does not exist — consistency at vertices is cheap compared with algebraizing 126 series.
